## Output contract

Print exactly one JSON object on stdout, and nothing after it. Its shape:

```json
{
  "version": 1,
  "items": [
    {"id": "n1", "match": "{{.ExampleType}}-k3x9q2", "conflict": ""},
    {"id": "n2", "match": "", "conflict": ""}
  ]
}
```

Rules, checked by Raun without exception:

- Every item of `new` appears exactly once.
- `match` is the ID of an item of `existing` of the same type, or `""` when the knowledge base does not hold the new item yet.
- `conflict` is `""` unless the new item contradicts the content of the item it matches. An item without a match has no conflict.
- There is no field for content or evidence: you only match. No other fields are accepted.
